# Interface naming convention

All TypeScript interfaces must use an **`I` prefix**.

## ✅ Good

```ts
interface IStoreResponse {
	id: string;
}
```

## ❌ Avoid

```ts
interface StoreResponse {
	id: string;
}
```

Applies to interfaces in standalone `.ts` files and in `<script setup lang="ts">` blocks in `.vue` files. API types live in `utils/types/api/` (e.g. `apiGo.ts`).
